B.A.T.M.A.N Talk and Workshop at wireless community weekend 07 in Graz/Austria

At the wireless community weekend 07 in Graz / Austria will be an open 
presentation, discussions and workshops covering the current state of the 
B.A.T.M.A.N mesh routing protocol.

There will be a general introduction into the protocol mechanisms and its 
capabilities during the mesh routing-protocols slot at Saturday, September 
15th at 5 pm.

We have also setup an experimental mesh network at the exhibition area with 
about 20 nodes running OLSR (0.5.4pre) and BATMAN (batman-0.2 and 
batman-experimental) in parallel.

On Sunday, September 16th (as well as anytime between) will be time for 
real-live experience during the hands-on workshops at 2 pm.

The event will take place at the Kunsthaus Graz in the city center.

See http://wiki.graz.funkfeuer.at/WirelessCommunityWeekend for further 
details.
